WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:06.220
A multimeter is a tool used to measure electrical
current, specifically voltage, current, and

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.380
resistance.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:12.650
To demonstrate how one of these works, I have
a computer open, and I will test this on the

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.730
power supply.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.830
If I get a reading, this should be good.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.630
If not, I would want to replace this power
supply.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:24.420
I'm not getting a reading, so this power supply
needs to be replaced.

